WEBVTT

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.860
I bought so much stuff online.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.050
This coffin's starting to look really nice.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:17.740
<b>D'oh</b>

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.990
There's not enough room...

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:54.510
<b>Episode 3</b>

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:54.510
<b>The Vampire Goes to School</b>

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:58.990
Okay, then, see you later.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.330
Good morning, Sophie-chan.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:06.900
You look tired.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.560
I couldn't sleep very well.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:12.380
I guess summer is close, huh?

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:13.740
It's not that.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.360
It was the pressure.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.730
Pressure?

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.360
<b>Squeeze</b>

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:22.610
I just finished talking to Hinata-chan.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.960
Her parents are away on vacation, 
and she's feeling lonely.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:28.660
I was about to go over and visit her.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:30.550
You should come, too!

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:34.960
Going to visit a friend's house? 
You have such a fulfilling social life.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:35.830
I do?

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.420
What kind of outfit should I wear?

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.520
Something formal?

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.980
<b>Blood</b>

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:47.980
Or something that lets me move freely?

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:52.220
I think this would be great.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.480
Looks like regular clothes are fine.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.700
<i>She trusts Google more than me?!</i>

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:01.620
Do we need anything else?

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.740
Should we bring her something, like a melon?

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.330
Don't worry about it.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:13.140
It's evening, but I still 
don't want to be careless.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.250
Stay on your guard.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.410
We're here, Sophie-chan!

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:20.560
Wow, so this Hinata's house.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.510
I'm so glad you came!

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.100
Thanks for having us.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.170
Come on in, Sophie.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.890
May I come in?

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.520
Of course!

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.390
I've been waiting for you two.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.640
What's wrong?

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.480
I've stepped into a friend's house!

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.290
How moving!

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:51.870
Just come in already.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.750
It's Mikan-chan!

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.120
This is our dog, Mikan!

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.540
Cute, huh?

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.090
Aww! Good puppy!

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:06.260
She loves everyone!

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:07.920
Really?

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.910
Didn't you just say she loves everyone?!

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:13.790
I guess she thinks you're an intruder.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:15.710
Probably because you're wearing all black.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:23.070
You guys can sit and relax. 
I'll bring some drinks.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.760
I'll help you.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.580
So this is a human bed, huh?

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:43.570
Once you get used to coffins, 
beds just don't feel right.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:46.000
With no walls and no lid,

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.570
I feel like I'd fall off in my sleep.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.540
<b>Tasty Potato Chips</b>

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.540
Lightly Salted

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:53.740
I'm really sorry we don't 
have any blood in the house.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:55.180
Don't worry about it.

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:58.360
But you came all the way here.
I have to offer you something...

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.060
I know!

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:03.050
Why don't I bring my little 
brother over here?

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:05.130
He's still young, so he's probably delicious.

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.480
Uh, that's okay.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.020
You should cherish him more.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:11.770
So Mikage-kun isn't with your parents?

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:15.780
I assumed you were all alone here 
since you said you were lonely.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:18.030
Yeah, but all he does is play games.

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:20.040
He doesn't pay any attention to me.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.030
Just like earlier...

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:25.900
It sure is lonely without Mom and Dad here.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.340
They'll be back tomorrow.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:29.940
I know!

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:34.340
Mikage!

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:41.830
I found these popsicles in the 
freezer. Let's eat them together!

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.890
Those were both mine!
I bought the second one for tomorrow!

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:48.150
So he said.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:51.570
After I tried to be nice by 
bringing him a popsicle...

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:52.930
Maybe it's his rebellious phase?

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:56.250
<i>Could these chips also be...</i>

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.000
But you know, everyone in your 
family gets along with each other.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.500
You think so?

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.470
But it's the same in your family, too.

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.670
I argue with my dad a lot.

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.130
Really?

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:16.820
I used to decorate the whole 
house with my favorite dolls.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:23.140
But it seems Dad doesn't really like dolls,

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:26.340
so he always yells at me to put them away.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.490
They're so cute, though!

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.060
My dad's such a weirdo.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:34.660
Well... there are people 
who don't like dolls, I guess.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:35.830
<b>Was previously traumatized</b>

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:37.530
That reminds me.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:41.200
I've never heard anything about 
your family, Sophie-chan.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:43.220
My family?

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.150
Yeah!

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:46.870
Your mother must be so pretty!

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:52.800
<b>Mid-Fantasy</b>

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:49.560
If you have any sisters,

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:52.800
I bet they also look like dolls!

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:56.130
When I was human, I did have a family,

00:06:56.130 --> 00:06:59.510
but since I'm the only one who became 
a vampire, I no longer have one.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:04.150
I'm sorry!

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.390
That was so insensitive of me!

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.630
No, don't worry about it.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:09.870
You don't have to feel so bad.

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:13.680
I know someone who became a vampire

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:16.750
and took her whole family down with her.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:18.750
"Took down"?

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:21.720
<i>I'm turning you into a vampire, too!</i>

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:25.990
That's terrifying.

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:30.760
That whole family is still
living together as vampires.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.440
Really?

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:35.540
She just posted a photo on 
Instagram a few days ago.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:39.310
My sister's 421st birthday!

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:39.300
That's a surprisingly heartwarming story.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:41.570
But you know...

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:44.950
If it happened to everybody, 
that could be fun.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.430
It's not that great, apparently.

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:54.200
<b>My sister's 421st birthday!</b>

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:51.930
You'll spend the rest of 
your existence looking

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.200
the way you did when you 
turned into a vampire.

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:57.950
<i>I know it's too late to do anything 
now, but it would've been nice</i>

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:00.970
<i>if you'd turned me into a vampire 
before my hair started thinning.</i>

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:03.030
<i>And before I started to get wrinkles.</i>

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:07.150
<i>Couldn't you have turned me into a 
vampire after my boobs got bigger?</i>

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:08.490
<i>I'm sorry, everyone.</i>

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:12.430
They've been complaining 
for hundreds of years now.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:14.750
I guess that would bring you down.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.090
Interesting.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:22.640
I've gotten completely 
accustomed to living by myself,

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:26.530
but hearing your stories makes it 
sound fun to be part of a family.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:30.070
Then you can think of me 
as you mother for today!

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:34.170
A mother who's over 300 
years younger than her child?

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:36.530
I haven't even seen that in light novels.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:39.400
I look older than you, so it's fine!

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:44.210
So the story is that you're 
a thirteen-year-old girl

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:47.580
who's out shopping with her mother.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.320
<i>But if she's a mother, doesn't that mean...</i>

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.090
<b>Husband</b>

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:54.060
<i>Akari is already someone's wife?!</i>

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:58.330
I'm not going to give my Akari 
to someone I know nothing about!

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:01.190
Oh, does this mean you're Akari's father?

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:04.830
This is getting complicated, 
so why don't we just say

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:07.100
that we're Sophie-chan's older sisters?

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.680
Hinata-chan, you'll be the oldest sister.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:12.800
Sisters... That sounds like fun!

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:15.190
<i>Onee-chan!</i>

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:19.810
<i>I bet having two younger sisters 
would make life exciting.</i>

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:21.290
Over here!

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:26.110
Come right into your big sister's arms!

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:23.250
<b>Lovey dovey</b>

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:23.950
<b>Fuss fuss</b>

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:24.710
<b>Lovey dovey</b>

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:25.410
<b>Fuss fuss</b>

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.120
<b>Lovey dovey</b>

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:28.880
Why only the baby sister?! No fair!

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:32.090
Sorry about that, Hinata-chan.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.580
I guess we said we're playing three sisters.

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:37.370
Okay, Sophie-chan, talk like a little sister

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:39.840
and call us "Onee-chan."

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:43.250
<i>How do little sisters talk?</i>

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:45.560
<i>I wonder if there are any references...</i>

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.300
<i>Maybe like this?</i>

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:54.060
How do you do, Onee-sama?

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:56.210
I think you've been watching too much anime.

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:02.480
Your tie is crooked, my petite soeur.

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:04.060
She's totally into this.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:08.450
If we're talking about 
families, pets are nice, too.

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:11.830
Mikan's a lot friendlier 
than my little brother.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:20.200
Well, dogs... are kind of 
scary when they bark.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:22.310
A cat could be good, though.

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:25.660
Oh, yeah, a black cat would 
probably suit you really well!

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:27.970
Meow!

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:30.670
Then why don't I be the cat?

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:31.590
Or maybe...

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:35.420
Look, I'm a cat. I'm really friendly!

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:38.370
You've been acting really 
weird this whole time.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:41.450
Well, uh, um...

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:45.690
You're not alone, Sophie-chan!

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:49.780
When I was human, I did have a family,

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:53.130
but since I'm the only one who became 
a vampire, I no longer have one.

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:57.680
Hearing your stories makes it 
sound fun to be part of a family.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:00.550
I won't ever let you feel lonely!

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:04.670
<i>Oh... She still feels bad about what she said.</i>

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:09.060
You're right. I have you now.

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:15.060
I even become someone with a real social 
life, someone who visits their friends.

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:19.040
You mean you'd never gone over 
to a friend's house before?

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:22.770
You're welcome to come 
here whenever you want.

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:25.140
You should visit me at my family's house, too!

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:27.570
That reminds me.

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:30.320
Wow!

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:32.790
I found this while I was cleaning my room.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:32.790
<b>Beating the bullies at the park!! Catching rhinoceros beetles!!
Two sleepyheads Excitable duo at the pool</b>

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:34.450
This brings back memories!

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:37.640
Looking at this, we really 
do look like sisters.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:41.840
<b>Catching rhinoceros beetles!!</b>

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:41.830
More like older brother and little sister.

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:44.440
Just kidding.

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:48.430
Maybe our plan to be three 
sisters was wrong, then.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:50.970
You too, Akari?

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:54.440
See you next time!

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:55.600
Yeah, see you!

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:00.760
Mikan...

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:02.650
She's asleep.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:09.130
It's even more lonely when everyone goes home.

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:15.660
I was probably too cold to her earlier.

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:19.930
Nee-chan?

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:20.870
Yeah?

00:12:21.810 --> 00:12:23.600
What's up, Mikage?

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.850
I'll make dinner tonight.

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:26.990
Are you sure?

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:27.940
Yeah.

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:30.830
Wait, those chips...

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:32.680
They were in the living room.

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:35.600
You forgot to eat them, 
so we ate them for you!

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:38.220
Then I guess you won't need dinner.

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:40.570
Wha?!

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:43.090
Why? Wait... Mikage!

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:53.570
So many manga characters are in high school.

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:56.930
A day in the life of a high school 
girl must be wonderful.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:12:59.850
Going home together after school...

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:02.020
<i>Look, a new place!</i>

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:03.940
<i>Let's take a peek!</i>

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:06.530
After-school clubs...

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:09.360
<i>I got us donuts!</i>

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:11.430
<i>Well, let's get started.</i>

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:14.460
Compared to that, my life is just...

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.980
The computer, going for walks...

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:19.960
Watching TV now and then...

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:23.120
Tending my bonsai, something my 
neighbor Tanabe-san suggested...

00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:30.210
<i>A bonsai is a friend.</i>

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:33.950
Except for the computer, that's just like 
the elderly people in my neighborhood!

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:36.680
School, huh?

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:40.790
I did go for that short time, 
but it didn't really suit me.

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:44.170
The classrooms got excessive 
amounts of sunlight.

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:46.670
Flying in the hallways was forbidden.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:51.150
I should get to sleep.

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:55.810
Huh?

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:59.010
Looks like Akari forgot her lunch.

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:02.370
Well, I guess she'll buy something there.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:12.020
<i>Today's omelet turned out really good!</i>

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:15.350
<i>And my octopus sausages 
turned out super cute, too!</i>

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:19.250
Nope, this is bugging me.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.540
I can't sleep.

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:28.660
Looks like I made it just in 
time for their lunch break.

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:38.230
Who is that?!

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.080
Is that an assassin?

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.260
An assassin? A real one?!

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:43.610
Oh, no! It's an assassin!

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:47.810
<i>I knew this outfit would raise suspicions.</i>

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:49.810
Oh, Sophie-chan!

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:51.940
What are you doing here?

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:54.500
Oh, I guess she's a friend of Amano-san's.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:56.130
That makes sense, then.

00:14:56.130 --> 00:14:58.370
That show on TV last night was so funny!

00:14:56.760 --> 00:15:00.410
Akari, what exactly do 
people here think of you?

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:00.410
What show? What happened?

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:02.990
I came to bring you your lunch.

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:04.900
You forgot it at home.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.610
Really?

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:07.750
Thank you!

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:12.230
But was it safe to walk around in 
the middle of the day by yourself?

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:14.870
It got a little scary partway,

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:18.420
but only my hair turned to ash.

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:21.910
Y-Your beautiful hair!

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:25.890
Please don't put yourself 
in such danger for me!

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:29.030
So this is the Sophie-chan 
you're always talking about?

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:30.700
That's right.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:34.890
Sophie-chan, these are my friends, 
Sakuya-chan and Yuu-chan.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:37.830
<b>{blue} Yuu-chan</b>

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:37.830
<b>Sakuya-chan</b>

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:36.840
Nice to meet you!

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:37.820
Nice to meet you.

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:39.240
Nice to meet you, too.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:41.330
Sophie-chan's a vampire, you know.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:44.100
You mean she really likes 
tomato juice, or what?

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:46.540
Or that her skin's so sensitive, 
she can't handle any sun?

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:49.270
No, I mean she turns to ash in the sunlight,

00:15:49.270 --> 00:15:51.000
and she has no reflection in mirrors.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:52.890
A real one?!

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:54.980
It's true! She doesn't have a reflection!

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:57.190
Wow, so you <i>are</i> one!

00:15:57.190 --> 00:15:58.210
Yeah.

00:15:58.210 --> 00:16:00.060
You're so cute.

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:03.330
You look just like a doll.

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:05.440
Exactly like Akari-chan said.

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:07.040
I told you so!

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:09.310
I wish I had a little sister like you.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:10.970
Me, too.

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:13.840
Hey, you have me!

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:16.190
Why are you mad? I was just agreeing with you.

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:15.890
<b>Grr</b>

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:18.680
She might not look like it,

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:20.910
but Sophie-chan is actually 
way older than us.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.670
Really?

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.750
So how old are you?

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:27.280
Um... Well...

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:31.260
Somewhere around 340 years old, I think.

00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:34.950
Stop looking at me like that.

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:36.660
<i>She lied about her age...</i>

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:38.220
<b>Actually 360 years old</b>

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:41.300
I'll get going now.

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:42.350
Wait!

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:45.890
Wouldn't it be safer if you waited 
here until the sun went down?

00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:48.030
Then we can just go home together.

00:16:48.030 --> 00:16:51.880
But if I wander around here 
all day in this outfit,

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:54.300
I'll become one of your 
school's seven legends.

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:57.540
Not to mention, I don't have a place 
to sit here in the classroom.

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:03.930
You can sit here.

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:05.000
No, thank you.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:08.100
Sorry... I couldn't help but overhear.

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:10.770
Yamada-san?

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:14.470
Would you mind standing in for 
me through the afternoon?

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:18.650
My sister is sick, and I want to 
go home early and check on her.

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:21.460
But my build and hair color 
are nothing like yours.

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:22.930
Won't people notice right away?

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:24.200
It'll be fine!

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:25.840
Your robe will prevent that!

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:28.670
Isn't wearing a robe already giving it away?

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:31.120
There we go.

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:33.920
Now you really look like a high school girl.

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:35.800
I guess, but...

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:36.780
<b>Ended up agreeing to do it</b>

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:38.160
It looks great on you!

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:41.790
So how does it feel, 
wearing our uniform?

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:45.540
<i>I'm trying to pass as a high school student,</i>

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.340
<i>so I should try answering like one.</i>

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:48.980
Um... Yeah!

00:17:50.550 --> 00:17:52.730
It feels tubular.

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:54.410
Totally connected to the now.

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:56.680
Tubular? What does that mean?

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:57.770
What?

00:17:57.770 --> 00:17:59.720
I read about that in a book once.

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.800
Those are sayings from an ancient time.

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:05.630
Just what you'd expect 
from an immortal vampire!

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:07.920
<i>I guess people don't say that anymore...</i>

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:10.000
Matsuda-san.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:10.740
Here.

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:12.530
Norikawa-san.

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:13.640
Here.

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:15.120
Yamada-san.

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:16.000
Yes.

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:18.800
Here.

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:20.810
<i>Who on earth is that?</i>

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:23.200
Excuse me.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:24.650
I'm Yamada.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.410
No, what I mean is...

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.000
I'm Yamada.

00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:32.380
<i>Since she's insisting, maybe it's true...</i>

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.750
<i>I can't see her face very well,</i>

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:37.430
<i>but there must be a reason 
for that strange outfit, too.</i>

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:40.300
Well, let's start class, then.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.420
She managed to fool her.

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:45.340
The colors of the flowers...

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:45.340
<b>Kokin Wakashu</b>

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:47.450
<i>I'm so sleepy.</i>

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:50.280
<i>Normally, I'd be asleep now.</i>

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:55.840
<i>But now, I'm sitting in a classroom 
impersonating a student named Yamada.</i>

00:18:56.390 --> 00:19:00.350
<i>I can't fall asleep and 
besmirch her good reputation.</i>

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:04.300
We'll stop there for today.

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:07.570
Yamada-san, you did very well 
to stay awake this entire lesson,

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:09.500
even though it's after lunch break.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:10.930
Well, for <i>you</i>, I mean.

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:13.130
<i>I should've slept!</i>

00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:16.590
Let's kill some time before the sun goes down.

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:20.360
This building is so dimly lit.
It's very comfortable.

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:23.550
Come to think of it, 
this dim section of the hall

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:27.260
happens to be the site of one 
of this school's seven legends.

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:31.790
A shadow that comes out at night 
and roams the north wing!

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:35.100
S-Stop that! You're scaring Sophie-chan.

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:38.560
You're a vampire, but ghost stories scare you?

00:19:40.060 --> 00:19:43.500
I'm happy I was able to scare you so much.

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:46.660
Maybe I should tell you lots more!

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:47.820
No.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:50.540
<b>Library</b>

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:50.540
Should we study for our exams?

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:53.320
We have Japanese, English, 
world history, and math.

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:54.550
Which one should we do?

00:19:54.990 --> 00:19:56.890
All those choices are awful.

00:19:58.150 --> 00:20:00.230
Can I see your textbook for a bit?

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:01.470
Go ahead.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:06.550
<b>International History</b>

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:05.550
This takes me back.

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:09.920
An acquaintance actually took me to 
see Marie Antoinette's beheading.

00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:12.100
Incredible.

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:13.970
A-And what was it like?

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:16.020
<b>World History</b>

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:19.140
Look! It's amazing!

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:22.230
I guess it was amazing.

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:23.840
According to my acquaintance.

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:26.560
That's a pretty ambiguous comment,
for someone who saw it in person.

00:20:26.560 --> 00:20:28.110
France, huh?

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:30.040
I wish I could've seen that, too.

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:32.790
Your Japanese is really good, though.

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:38.020
Well, I never studied it, but I've 
been living in Japan for a long time.

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:39.400
I read a lot of books, too.

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:41.000
So you learned it all by yourself?

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:43.300
All right, then, here's a Japanese quiz.

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:45.010
What does "two birds with one stone" mean?

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:48.970
It means to gain two or more 
benefits through one action.

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:49.880
Correct!

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:51.170
What about "a drop in the bucket"?

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:53.640
An amount that is insignificantly small.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:54.880
Correct!

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:56.890
Okay, how about "blood will have blood"?

00:20:57.600 --> 00:21:00.960
It means extreme lavishness 
or gluttony, right?

00:21:00.960 --> 00:21:03.450
You misremembered that one.

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:07.680
I hope we can talk again soon, Sophie-chan!

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:08.650
Yeah.

00:21:08.650 --> 00:21:09.890
See you again.

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:11.410
See you tomorrow!

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:14.880
Oh, good. It looks like your 
hair has grown back.

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:18.030
I told you, it grows back 
once the sun goes down.

00:21:19.100 --> 00:21:22.040
That reminds me, I've got 
a favor to ask you two.

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:27.250
Did something just come out today?

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:28.220
No.

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:31.480
Stopping somewhere after school...

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:34.800
It's so... youthful.

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:36.230
I see.

00:21:36.780 --> 00:21:39.280
You do seem really happy!

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:51.970
<b>Episode 4</b>

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:51.970
<b>Sophie and Ellie</b>

00:23:13.440 --> 00:23:16.010
Today was so much fun!

00:23:16.010 --> 00:23:17.120
It's weird.

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:21.330
The only memories I had from 
school before were bad ones.

00:23:23.770 --> 00:23:26.430
That's because you're with me now, I bet.

00:23:30.350 --> 00:23:32.970
Oh... That makes sense.

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:37.440
You're going to make me blush
if you just accept it like that!

00:23:37.440 --> 00:23:39.280
Well, same goes for me...
